    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0286" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9229: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-21T12:00:00+01:00">March 21,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. The British Consul General informs me that he has heard from an official
                    source that 250 additional German members of the Armistice Commission are
                    shortly arriving in French Morocco. He hears that they will be distributed with
                    a view to obtaining a firm hold on the country.</p>
                <pb facs="0287" n="275" xml:id="pg275"/>
                <p>The British Consul General has been informed the purpose of Weygand’s present
                    visit to Morocco has been to concert with Noguès<anchor n="98" xml:id="d218-f1"
                    /> to prevent further infiltration. It is considered doubtful by my colleague
                    whether they can. He believes the farthest they will go in their reaction
                    against it will be to resign.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Casablanca.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d218-f1" n="98" xml:id="d218-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Albert Noguès, Resident General in the French Zone of Morocco.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
